A wizard doppleganger of mine has a per Archon. I find from
experimenting that they seem to judge armour merely by its numerical
enchantment, in general.
Therefore before trying any dangerous manouver, it might be a cunning
ploy to get it in a dead end and drop something a bit enchanted, e.g. a
+3 large or elven shield, or small one -if available. You'll find I
think that unless the Archon has at least a +4 (or more) silver shield
(unlikely) it will take your offering. You've upped it's defence a bit
numerically, but if it drops a silver shield you might be lucky with
wands ! Just a thought. Also try giving a boosted up mummy wrapping and
it might swap that for a more magical but numerically lower cloak.

